{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c383","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b368-b8fb-7503-b19c-2c040425ca00"},"sequence":28,"recorded_at":1780531400000051,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9c78dd5e-2606-42c8-9e04-207bbea54fed","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"9c78dd5e-2606-42c8-9e04-207bbea54fed","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9c78dd5e-2606-42c8-9e04-207bbea54fed"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b368-c919-79c0-bd78-94b4c51cbc1b"},"task_id":"01a0b368-c919-79c0-bd78-94b4c51cbc1b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b368-c919-79c0-bd78-94b4c51cbc1b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-32ypr2, status=development)' 2>&1; echo \\\"---\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-32ypr2/TASK-260830-32ypr2_producer.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Set status and read producer instructions\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"ok\\\":true,\\\"result\\\":{\\\"primary\\\":{\\\"action\\\":\\\"status_changed\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"TASK-260830-32ypr2\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"to-dev\\\"},\\\"side_effects\\\":[{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"STORY-260830-1cyj0q\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"integrating\\\"},{\\\"action\\\":\\\"escalated\\\",\\\"element_id\\\":\\\"EPIC-260830-391tge\\\",\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"new_value\\\":\\\"development\\\",\\\"old_value\\\":\\\"integrating\\\"}]}}\\n---\\nOwn TASK-260830-32ypr2 (test-unknown-encrypted-and-incomplete-events), the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q (canonical-session-capture-and-evidence, EPIC M4). Predecessors TASK-260830-24z2b3 (internal/clonebundle closed types, builders and decoders: Canonical Session/Event, Raw Object and Capture Manifests, Capture Boundary, blob install) and TASK-260830-2g5be6 (the capture operation over a real store, Stable Snapshot Proof, the source-race check before projection, workspace binding) are accepted and checkpointed on the Story branch. Your Change Request is the story_final whole-Story patch: read the whole branch delta (`git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree log --stat <trunk>..HEAD`) and both outcomes first. This leaf is the PROJECTION-FIDELITY closure of pinned Section 13.14.1, driven over captured bytes, not over hand-written Canonical Events: build the projection input with the predecessor's capture entry so every proof runs through the real path.\\nScope — four invariants, each driven and each mutated:\\n(1) Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events. A record whose native type is not in the closed kind registry projects to `opaque_event` with `opaque` visibility, keeps a Source Evidence whose raw blob/manifest byte-range references actually resolve back to the captured bytes (sorted, unique, in range), and is never dropped, guessed, coerced into a neighbouring kind or re-typed on a second projection (project twice and compare). Drive a record that is ALMOST a known kind (right envelope, unknown inner type) as well as a wholly unknown one.\\n(2) Foreign signed/encrypted reasoning stays opaque. A foreign encrypted or signed reasoning record projects to `opaque_reasoning`, is preserved byte-exact (its bytes survive a round trip through the blob store and back), is never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated or promoted to `reasoning_summary`, and never becomes higher-authority content. Foreign instructions remain LOW-AUTHORITY history: prove that an instruction carried in a foreign record cannot change the projected session's effective instruction snapshot or authority, and that source usage numbers never become target accounting.\\n(3) Incomplete tool calls never become live actions. Historical tools are inert: a `tool_definition_snapshot` projects as history and cannot register a callable tool; a `tool_call` without its `tool_result` becomes ABORTED history and blocks pending action — drive the whole matrix (call with result; call without result; result without call; call whose result arrives after the capture boundary; nested/subagent call) and assert the projected kind, the visibility and the \\\"no pending action\\\" property for each. A mutant that lets an incomplete call project as pending or callable must redden a test.\\n(4) The closed shapes that carry all of the above: Canonical Event's exact member set (zero-based contiguous ordinal, 0..64 sorted unique causal parents, Actor UUIDv7, nullable turn, kind from the closed 26-kind registry, nullable source time, public|projection|internal|opaque visibility, kind-selected closed payload, Source Evidence, extensions); Source Evidence with capture status exact|partial|synthesized|unavailable and stable reason codes, where a SYNTHESIZED event has no native Event ID and identifies the core operation that made it; message-like payloads using exactly the closed content blocks text|json|image|audio|document|resource_link|redacted|opaque with typed inline content or Blob Descriptor references and inline content at most 64 KiB (witness 65536 accepted and 65537 refused, and prove that oversized inline content becomes a blob reference rather than a silent truncation); Canonical Session bounds 1..1024 Actors, 1..1,000,000 ordered unique Event IDs, 1..1024 head IDs, an Actor's `parent` null only for `main`.\\nEvidence: every row driven through a production entry with a named committed test, an n-of-m ratio and call sites; a projection determinism proof (same captured bytes -> byte-identical canonical output twice); negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control; and a conformance matrix over every 13.14.1/10.2/7.8 clause this Story claims, mapped to a test, a stated bound or NOT APPLICABLE with its owner. State explicitly any part of 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity/lineage, bundle chain, transaction, events and tuple admission) that this Story does NOT own, so the matrix cannot be read as a wider claim.\\nCOMMON CONTRACT (FINAL leaf of its Story — your Change Request is the story_final whole-Story patch). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named above; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260917-110onn) may land on trunk during your run — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers and use the v0.7.0 artifacts everywhere the v0.6.0 ones are named below. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) and above all the packages your own Story's earlier leaves added on this branch — never fork a second model of anything already modeled; extend or adopt and say which. STORY-CLOSE ITEMS, all owned by this leaf: (a) internal/traceability ownership registry bindings for every normative section this Story claims plus the Story's acceptance case bound to the REAL conformance suite with honest coverage text that separates executed lanes from stated bounds (precedent Stories 3drr2m/3jqsx1/3m2mw8/2jylym/1kiyj6) — edit the ADOPTED registry, `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json` if the v0.7.0 adoption is on trunk when you refresh, otherwise `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`, and never invent a binding for a clause no test drives; (b) re-derive and re-pin `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in internal/traceability/traceability.go from the semantic JSON projection of the registry you just edited — derive it, never copy a digest from another Story, and show the derivation command and output in the results; (c) `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` green plus the section-scoped run for each section you bound, with the measured coverage ratio quoted verbatim in the results; (d) README: a section for each package this Story added with its exact test commands and NO capability or CLI claim (no `ax` command exists), and the \\\"Measured coverage of this repository\\\" subsection updated to the numbers tracecheck actually prints; (e) one newest-first LOGBOOK entry for the Story. The candidate's task-board.config.json must stay byte-identical to trunk unless you deliberately add a bounded validation command — if you add one, say so explicitly in the results and keep it fast. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write or an explicit purity bound; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test, a stated bound or NOT APPLICABLE with an owner. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q ALREADY EXISTS and its tip is the previous leaf's signed checkpoint commit — do not re-provision, rebase, commit on, amend or revert it, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept. Your candidate is the UNCOMMITTED working tree on top of that checkpoint; the CR the runtime builds from it is the WHOLE-Story patch, so read every earlier leaf's delta (`git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree log --stat <trunk>..HEAD`) and its outcome resources before you start. If origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree re