 assert the effect.\\n(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\\n(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \\\"Composes X\\\", \\\"never admits what decoding refuses\\\", \\\"nothing re-implemented\\\", \\\"no cached sentinel can authorize\\\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\\nFinally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.\\n\\nTRUNK STATE AT YOUR SPAWN (recorded 2026-09-18): origin/main is c3aae73 as of 2026-09-18T01:30Z and carries BOTH the v0.7.0 adoption (PR #52, commit 2fc6d50) and the mesh-RPC Story plus the resumesmoke deadline fix (PR #53 a12d1bd, PR #54 c3aae73) — internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md, internal/specpin/v0.7.0.lock.json, internal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json with `catalog.Adopted = ReleaseV070`, internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json, and traceability.go pointing at that trio. Cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers as the v0.6.0 sections named above. If origin/main moves again before your handoff, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate <this task>` and then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old base> <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`: README.md and LOGBOOK.md moved on trunk with that landing, so keep your edits purely additive on top of the NEW content and never restore the old bytes; task-board.config.json must end byte-identical to the new base.\\n\\nYOUR PREVIOUS ATTEMPT FAILED AT CR CONSTRUCTION FOR A PROVENANCE REASON, NOT FOR ANYTHING IN YOUR WORK — READ THIS FIRST. The construction refused with:\\n`delivery failure [stale-anchor]: change_request_base_authority_mismatch: the STORY-260830-1cyj0q candidate provenance disagrees: checkpoint 47294bb8 does not descend from selected authority c3aae73 while branch=47294bb8 and head=47294bb8`.\\nNothing about that is your content. The Story branch was cut before trunk advanced: its tip is the TASK-260830-2g5be6 checkpoint sitting on base a12d1bd, while current origin/main is c3aae73 (PR #54 landed STORY-260830-4qojoz, which also raised the configured suite from 27 to 30 commands). A Change Request must descend from the selected authority, so the branch has to move onto c3aae73 before any CR can be constructed here.\\nSo, BEFORE you do anything else: run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-32ypr2`. You are the live tracked producer for this initial leaf and it provably has no Change Request, which is exactly the case that command exists for; it preserves your complete working candidate exactly and replays the two checkpoints (TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev6 and TASK-260830-2g5be6 rev3) with signing in an isolated workspace. If a regular-file conflict appears, prepare `--replay-resolutions` from the retained replay worktree's `resolution-template.json`, binding each resolution to REBASE_HEAD, its unmerged path and the SHA-256 of the explicit replacement content — keep LOGBOOK entries newest-first and never resolve by discarding trunk content.\\nAfter the refresh, audit every path in `git diff --name-only a12d1bd c3aae73` that also appears in your `git status`: README.md, LOGBOOK.md and task-board.config.json all moved on trunk, so your edits must sit on top of the NEW content, never restore the old bytes, and the config must end byte-identical to the new base. Then read the command count from the candidate config rather than assuming it — it is 30 now, not 27.\\nEverything you already wrote in the worktree is preserved and still stands: start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state in your results what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of redoing it. Your scope is unchanged.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 17257,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4315,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
