`RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n+- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n+- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n \\n - DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n@@ 