/ error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n+- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n+- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n \\n - DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n@@ -45,6 +53,15 @@\\n - FIGURES: contracts=64, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=135, fixtures=33, historical contracts=55; bindings=68 (full=2, partial=6, sliver=4, unevidenced=52, unmeasured=4), unowned=7, discharged clauses=49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim anywhere.\\n - STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-219okr — dual-stack major negotiation (first leaf)\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/meshneg` (`Negotiate`/`LocalMajors`/`PeerOffer`/`Select` over `Refusal`/`Decision` pure data): generation-to-majors mapping (Config-1: 2; Config-2: 2,3; Config-3: 2,3,4; Config-4: exactly 5), single-major peer-offer validation against the framing major, highest-common selection, no-common-major refusal with registry-resolved `incompatible_protocol`/6 (unknown config: `invalid_config`/3), exact per-major contracts/namespaces/bound error versions rebuilt from rpcwire/axerror, and core-only peer exposure (`directory_mesh_unsupported`, `terminal_backend_unavailable`), never zero inventory. Frames nothing, admits nothing, pure/stateless. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- BINDING CHOICE: the RPC-4 exposure equivalent is the registered `terminal_backend_unavailable` (exit 6), not a minted token — Section 11.9 requires reporting evidence unsupported rather than empty and 17.4 requires reporting activation unavailable; the 1.3.0 exit-6 row carries exactly that code. Refusal/exposure exits resolve via `axerror.ExitCodeFor` under each code's introducing version; cross-version stability is asserted by test, not assumed.\\n+- MUTANTS: 27 narrowing probes killed by named tests (neutral passed, harmless Detail-text control SURVIVED as designed; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`). Two initial SURVIVEDs were test gaps the harness caught: substituted-keys (same count, caught by membership loop, not length check) and peer-mixing-1-beside-common (unobservable without overlap) — both closed with new cases before the evidence run. Successor run RUN-260917-244f06 re-executed the harness: 27 killed, neutral passed, control SURVIVED (exit 0), and corrected the earlier \\\"28\\\" count.\\n+- BOUNDS: v2 1-16 minor ranges select the major only (within-major minor selection future work); handshake sequencing stays with rpcwire decode + the responder; admission (identity/allowlist/generation) stays with TASK-260830-z1yxg9 with separation pinned by `TestNegotiationIsNotAdmission`; no `ax` command, doctor result, or capability claimed. Traceability registry/digest untouched for the story final leaf (package-local TRACEABILITY.md only).\\n+- AC: 11 of 11 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n+- REV3 (RUN-260917-27bea1): rev1/rev2 CR validation both failed at suite command 5/27 on the sessquery race-timeout (default 10m, load-dependent, leaf-independent); trunk `888ae3d` fixed it systemically with an explicit `-timeout 25m`. Refreshed the candidate onto `888ae3d` (`refresh_advanced`, config restored to HEAD by hand, production untouched) and ran the full 27-command suite once: all exits 0, race gate 38 ok with sessquery 515.663s and no DATA RACE, meshneg 87.8%, mutants 27 killed / neutral passed / control SURVIVED.\\n+- REV4 (RUN-260917-8fb798): rev3 review (RUN-260917-92b548) routed CHANGES REQUESTED with 3xP2 + 3xP3, all evidence/docs, production selection logic accepted unchanged. F1: exposure expectations now assert the literal `directory_mesh_unsupported` / `terminal_backend_unavailable` tokens at the Negotiate entry (no committed test derives from the production constants) + 2 same-exit swap plants. F2: new `TestNegotiateUnknownGeneration` drives unknown generations x every frame through Negotiate (invalid_config/3, zero Decision) + Negotiate-site fallback plant. F3: docs name `LoadedConfiguration.SourceVersion` (not the normalized SchemaVersion) + `TestLocalMajorsTracksConfigVocabulary` pins the mapping against config.Version1/Version2/CurrentVersion/Version4 with a Decode-level normalization proof. F4: stated bound (non-rpc arrays validated by rpcwire decode, trusted here; direct callers must pass decode-produced hellos) pinned by `TestPeerOfferTrustsDecodedNonRPCArrays`; probe showed v2 lease 9.9.9 is admitted by decode too (valid range by design, not a hole). F5: frame rows 4.1.0/5.0.1/5.1.0 + 5.x-edge plant + unparseable-class bound stated. F6: TRACEABILITY 17.1 minor clause dropped. Harness now 31 narrowing killed / neutral passed / control SURVIVED (exit 0); 18/18 package tests green; full 27-command suite green (38 ok verbose/race/cover, race sessquery 370.955s no DATA RACE, meshneg 87.8%).\\n+\\n ### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n - DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n - F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n===== worktree vs old HEAD: LOGBOOK =====\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 15ddafe..b7f6d16 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,15 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-18\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (matrix, invariants, 33-row refusal table plus the unstable and drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure); 44 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite. No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` upgraded unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `9b9516d7…339e0b6` via the production marshal path); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`