on: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the foreign instruction into the effective snapshot; every other foreign record stays history-only.\\nok: N-foreign-payload-authority: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the foreign high claim into the payload authority; every other foreign instruction still pins low.\\nok: N-tool-incomplete: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly call-7 without its result as completed; every other incomplete call still becomes aborted history.\\nok: N-tool-orphan: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the ghost orphan result as completed; every other orphan still becomes aborted history.\\nok: N-callable: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly evil-tool past the live-claim refusal and registers it callable; every other live claim still refuses.\\nok: N-callable-false: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly evt-def-1 as callable in the sealed payload; the token stays and every other definition still pins false.\\nok: N-pending-aborted: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the aborted call-7 as a pending action; every other aborted call still never pends.\\nok: N-pending-completed: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the completed call-1 as pending without a live work order; every other completed call still needs one.\\nok: N-live-followup: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the call-live followup claim; every other live followup still refuses.\\nok: N-duplicate-call: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the duplicated call-dup ID; every other duplicate call still refuses.\\nok: N-usage-target: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Funds the target ledger from exactly evt-use-1; every other source record still counts source-only.\\nok: N-overflow-bound: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly 65537-byte text inline past the 64 KiB bound; 65538+ still becomes a blob reference.\\nok: N-overflow-truncate: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Silently truncates oversized text to 64 KiB instead of installing a blob reference; the byte-exactness killer redden