comes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 48 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n+- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\n+- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n+- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\n+\n+### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\n","final_result":true}}}
